::CW_U06_L01_GP_Q01::Portfolio context: A writer says, "I chose this poem because I like it." What is the best revision of the selection reason?{
~A. I chose this poem because it was short.#Incorrect. Length alone is not craft evidence.
~B. I chose this poem because I found it first.#Incorrect. File order does not prove portfolio value.
=C. I chose this poem because the revised final image shows stronger control of imagery and emotion.#Correct. This gives a craft-based reason supported by revision evidence.
~D. I chose no pieces because portfolios do not need writing.#Incorrect. A portfolio requires selected work.
}

::CW_U06_L01_GP_Q02::Which item is the strongest evidence for a craft rationale?{
=A. A before-and-after revision that changes "I was lonely" into a specific bus stop image.#Correct. This shows a concrete revision and craft improvement.
~B. A statement that the piece exists.#Incorrect. Existence is not evidence of craft growth.
~C. A random font change.#Incorrect. Random formatting does not show craft rationale.
~D. A sentence saying the piece is good.#Incorrect. This is vague praise, not evidence.
}

::CW_U06_L01_GP_Q03::Which three parts belong in a complete craft rationale?{
~A. Title, font, and file name.#Incorrect. These do not explain craft growth.
~B. Summary, summary, and more summary.#Incorrect. A rationale needs evidence and effect, not only summary.
~C. Favorite line, favorite color, and page number.#Incorrect. These do not form a complete rationale.
=D. Selection claim, evidence, and reader effect.#Correct. These parts explain why the piece belongs in the portfolio.
}

::CW_U06_L01_GP_Q04::A writer revised direct emotion into an image. What should the rationale explain?{
~A. That revision does not matter.#Incorrect. The revision is central evidence.
=B. How the image helps the reader infer the emotion instead of being told directly.#Correct. This connects craft evidence to reader effect.
~C. That the image was chosen randomly.#Incorrect. A rationale should show purpose.
~D. That readers should ignore the image.#Incorrect. The image is important evidence.
}

::CW_U06_L01_GP_Q05::Which rationale is weakest?{
~A. I selected this story because the revised dialogue reveals conflict more clearly.#Incorrect. This is a craft-based rationale.
~B. I selected this poem because the line breaks now slow the reader at the final image.#Incorrect. This explains craft effect.
=C. I selected this piece because it is nice and I like it.#Correct. This is weakest because it gives vague praise without evidence.
~D. I selected this script because feedback helped me add speaker labels that clarify performance.#Incorrect. This uses revision evidence.
}
